div.p:
—What started as a popular movement for Moroccans and the King in late 1975 has
                    now turned into a risky venture in which many, including perhaps the King
                    himself, perceive the monarchy to be in trouble, and under attack;

—King Hassan has been angered by American refusal of arms for the Sahara war but
                    at the same time he seems to appreciate the fact that U.S. arms cannot turn the
                    war around in his favor;

—support for and good relations with a strong, moderate Morocco free of its
                    conflict in the Western Sahara and thereby free to play a more active role in
                    the peace process;
